{"abstract":"Examining the influence of structural holes and closed networks on innovation performance, this paper argues that closed networks are more favorable for innovation performance than open networks. Based on a comprehensive theoretical overview of characteristics, we suggest that a lower number of structural holes will augment the innovation performance of networking firms in our sample of R&D alliances in the consumer electronics industry. Potential benefits of both the structural holes theory as well as the opposing network approach of closed networks contribute to this proposition. Our findings also show that closed networks increase innovation performance in R&D networks. Thereby, we suggest that the prevalence of mainly collectivist-oriented players in this industry has influenced our results due to the specific cultural contexts and environments of the collaborating firms.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Scherer, Susanne","Puck, Jonas","Glowik, Mario","Binder, Gregor","Lindner, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-297214"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Audencia Business School","Audi AG","Berlin School of Economics and Law","Deloitte Austria","University of Innsbruck","Vienna University of Economics and Business"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innovation performance in collectivist societies a network perspective","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-297214","identifier":[{"id":"85174192870","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-e561daf3-a812-4854-864e-871274f5dfe4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A13E2C8D5CEFFE95ED6368504D8923F9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"audi ag","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Audi AG","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"vienna university of economics and business","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vienna University of Economics and Business","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"berlin school of economics and law","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Berlin School of Economics and Law","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"at","key":"deloitte austria","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Deloitte Austria","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Finance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"fr","key":"audencia business school","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Audencia Business School","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"schererpau","last":"Scherer","name":"Scherer, Susanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"puckpau","last":"Puck","name":"Puck, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"glowikpau","last":"Glowik","name":"Glowik, Mario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregor","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Gregor","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"lindnerpau","last":"Lindner","locid":"e655aefa-2a8c-4554-b388-a514aab30d4b","name":"Lindner, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-0203-9112","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Desislava","key":"dikovapedh","last":"Dikova","name":"Dikova, Desislava","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Edith","key":"ipsmillerpedh","last":"Ipsmiller","name":"Ipsmiller, Edith","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781800882942.00012","eisbn":["9781800882942"],"isbn":["9781800882935"],"pages":"114-134","place":"Cheltenham","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","series":"Research Handbooks in Business and Management","status":"p","title":"Research Handbook on Innovation in International Business"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-e561daf3-a812-4854-864e-871274f5dfe4"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Innovation Performance in Collectivist Societies : A Network Perspective","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-297214","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The flux of high-energy neutrinos passing through the Earth is attenuated due to their interactions with matter. The interaction rate is determined by the neutrino interaction cross section and affects the flux arriving at the IceCube Neutrino Observatory, a cubic-kilometer neutrino detector embedded in the Antarctic ice sheet. We present a measurement of the neutrino cross section between 60 TeV and 10 PeV using the high-energy starting event (HESE) sample from IceCube with 7.5 years of data. The result is binned in neutrino energy and obtained using both Bayesian and frequentist statistics. We find it compatible with predictions from the Standard Model. While the cross section is expected to be flavor independent above 1 TeV, additional constraints on the measurement are included through updated experimental particle identification (PID) classifiers, proxies for the three neutrino flavors. This is the first such measurement to use a ternary PID observable and the first to account for neutrinos from tau decay.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Abbasi, R.","Ackermann, M.","Adams, J.","Aguilar, J. A.","Ahlers, Markus Tobias","Ahrens, M.","Alispach, C.","Alves, A. A.","Amin, N. M.","Andeen, K.","Anderson, T.","Ansseau, I","Anton, G.","Arguelles, C.","Axani, S.","Bai, X.","Balagopal, A.","Barbano, A.","Barwick, S. W.","Bastian, B.","Basu, Alakananda","Baum, Oliver","Baur, S.","Bay, R.","Beatty, J. J.","Becker, K-H","Tjus, J. Becker","Bellenghi, C.","BenZvi, S.","Berley, D.","Bernardini, E.","Besson, D. Z.","Binder, G.","Bindig, D.","Blaufuss, E.","Blot, S.","Boeser, S.","Botner, O.","Boettcher, J.","Bourbeau, Etienne","Bourbeau, J.","Bradascio, F.","Braun, J.","Bron, S.","Brostean-Kaiser, J.","Burgman, A.","Busse, R. S.","Koskinen, D. Jason","Rameez, M","Stuttard, Thomas Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Icecube Collaboration"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Italy","Japan","Russia","Sweden","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chiba Univ, Chiba University, Inst Global Prominent Res","DESY, Helmholtz Association, Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron (DESY)","Free University of Brussels","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","Harvard University","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Karlsruhe Inst Technol, Helmholtz Association, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Inst Kernphys","Loyola Univ Chicago, Loyola University Chicago, Dept Phys","Marquette University","Moscow Engineering Physics Institute","Ohio State University","RWTH Aachen University","South Dakota Sch Mines & Technol, South Dakota School Mines & Technology, Phys Dept","Stockholm University","Technical University of Munich","Univ Delaware, University of Delaware, Dept Phys & Astron","Univ Wuppertal, University of Wuppertal, Dept Phys","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Irvine","University of Geneva","University of Maryland, College Park","University of Münster","University of Padua","University of Rochester","University of Wisconsin-Madison","University of Würzburg","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Acceleration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measurement of the high energy all flavor neutrino nucleon cross section with icecube","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.104.022001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471625","identifier":[{"id":"85110694984","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000671589000001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-82af3ba3-8500-4b01-a842-a366eb272199"