hysrevd.104.022001","issn":["15502368","24700010"],"issn_org":["24700010"],"issue":"2","journal":"Physical Review D","paperid":"022001","status":"p","title":"Physical Review D","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85110694984"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82af3ba3-8500-4b01-a842-a366eb272199"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measurement of the high-energy all-flavor neutrino-nucleon cross section with IceCube","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471625","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A recent time-integrated analysis of a catalog of 110 candidate neutrino sources revealed a cumulative neutrino excess in the data collected by IceCube between 2008 April 6 and 2018 July 10. This excess, inconsistent with the background hypothesis in the Northern Hemisphere at the 3.3 sigma level, is associated with four sources: NGC 1068, TXS 0506+056, PKS 1424+240, and GB6 J1542+6129. This Letter presents two time-dependent neutrino emission searches on the same data sample and catalog: a point-source search that looks for the most significant time-dependent source of the catalog by combining space, energy, and time information of the events, and a population test based on binomial statistics that looks for a cumulative time-dependent neutrino excess from a subset of sources. Compared to previous time-dependent searches, these analyses enable a feature to possibly find multiple flares from a single direction with an unbinned maximum-likelihood method. M87 is found to be the most significant time-dependent source of this catalog at the level of 1.7 sigma post-trial, and TXS 0506+056 is the only source for which two flares are reconstructed. The binomial test reports a cumulative time-dependent neutrino excess in the Northern Hemisphere at the level of 3.0 sigma associated with four sources: M87, TXS 0506+056, GB6 J1542+6129, and NGC 1068.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Abbasi, R.","Ackermann, M.","Adams, J.","Ahlers, Markus Tobias","Anderson, T.","Binder, G.","Bourbeau, Etienne","Braun, J.","Chen, C.","Dittmer, M.","Engel, R.","Evans, J.","Fischer, L.","Garcia, A.","Goldschmidt, A.","Hoffmann, R.","Jansson, M.","Jones, B. J. P.","Kang, D.","Karl, M.","Klein, S. R.","Koskinen, D. Jason","Kozynets, Tetiana","Larson, M. J.","Lee, J. W.","Li, Y.","Liu, Q. R.","Lyu, Y.","Madsen, J.","Mead, James","Meier, M.","Park, N.","Paul, L.","Peters, L.","Plum, M.","Rameez, M","Rehman, A.","Reusch, S.","Sarkar, S.","Sarkar, S.","Schmidt, T.","Schneider, A.","Sharma, A.","Stuttard, Thomas Simon","Weiss, M. J.","Wolf, M.","Xu, X. W.","Xu, Y.","Yu, S.","Zhang, Z."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482116"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corpau":["Icecube Collaboration"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DESY, Helmholtz Association, Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron (DESY)","Loyola Univ Chicago, Loyola University Chicago, Dept Phys"],"keyword":["Jets","MODEL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"search for multi flare neutrino emissions in 000000000010 yr of icecube data from a catalog of sources","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2109.05818.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-482116","identifier":[{"id":"000710436900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85118268085","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-94755ea2-e75f-45a6-912e-102fa90df425"],"keyword":["ASTROPHYSICAL SOURCES","BLAZAR TXS 0506+056","COINCIDENT","JETS","M87","MODEL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8C4A55343D76125685F6C40FBC70316B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2109.05818.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"loyola univ chicago loyola university chicago dept phys","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Loyola Univ Chicago, Loyola University Chicago, Dept Phys","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"desy helmholtz association deutsches elektronen synchrotron","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"