"first":"M. J.","key":"weissmjpau","last":"Weiss","name":"Weiss, M. J.","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"wolfmpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, M.","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"X. W.","key":"xuxwpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, X. W.","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Y.","key":"xuypau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Y.","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S.","key":"yuspau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, S.","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Z.","key":"zhangzpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Z.","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3847/2041-8213/ac2c7b","issn":["20418205","20418213"],"issn_org":["20418205"],"issue":"2","journal":"Astrophysical Journal Letters","paperid":"45","status":"p","title":"Astrophysical Journal Letters","volume":"920"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118268085"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-94755ea2-e75f-45a6-912e-102fa90df425"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Search for Multi-flare Neutrino Emissions in 10 yr of IceCube Data from a Catalog of Sources","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482116","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The IceCube Neutrino Observatory has established the existence of a high-energy all-sky neutrino flux of astrophysical origin. This discovery was made using events interacting within a fiducial region of the detector surrounded by an active veto and with reconstructed energy above 60 TeV, commonly known as the high-energy starting event sample (HESE). We revisit the analysis of the HESE sample with an additional 4.5 years of data, newer glacial ice models, and improved systematics treatment. This paper describes the sample in detail, reports on the latest astrophysical neutrino flux measurements, and presents a source search for astrophysical neutrinos. We give the compatibility of these observations with specific isotropic flux models proposed in the literature as well as generic power-law-like scenarios. Assuming v(e): v(mu): v(tau) = 1:1:1, and an equal flux of neutrinos and antineutrinos, we find that the astrophysical neutrino spectrum is compatible with an unbroken power law, with a preferred spectral index of 2.87(-0.19)(+0.20) for the 68% confidence interval.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Abbasi, R.","Ackermann, M.","Adams, J.","Aguilar, J. A.","Ahlers, Markus Tobias","Ahrens, M.","Alispach, C.","Alves, A. A.","Amin, N. M.","Andeen, K.","Anderson, T.","Ansseau, I","Anton, G.","Arguelles, C.","Axani, S.","Bai, X.","Balagopal, A.","Barbano, A.","Barwick, S. W.","Bastian, B.","Basu, Alakananda","Baum, Oliver","Baur, S.","Bay, R.","Beatty, J. J.","Becker, K-H","Tjus, J. Becker","Bellenghi, C.","BenZvi, S.","Berley, D.","Bernardini, E.","Besson, D. Z.","Binder, G.","Bindig, D.","Blaufuss, E.","Blot, S.","Boeser, S.","Botner, O.","Boettcher, J.","Bourbeau, Etienne","Bourbeau, J.","Bradascio, F.","Braun, J.","Bron, S.","Brostean-Kaiser, J.","Burgman, A.","Busse, R. S.","Koskinen, D. Jason","Rameez, M","Stuttard, Thomas Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545941"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Icecube Collaboration"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Italy","Russia","Sweden","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DESY, Helmholtz Association, Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron (DESY)","Free University of Brussels","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","Harvard University","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Karlsruhe Inst Technol, Helmholtz Association, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Inst Kernphys","Loyola Univ Chicago, Loyola University Chicago, Dept Phys","Marquette University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Moscow Engineering Physics Institute","Ohio State University","RWTH Aachen University","South Dakota Sch Mines & Technol, South Dakota School Mines & Technology, Phys Dept","Stockholm University","Technical University of Munich","Univ Delaware, University of Delaware, Dept Phys & Astron","Univ Wuppertal, University of Wuppertal, Dept Phys","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Irvine","University of Geneva","University of Maryland, College Park","University of Münster","University of Padua","University of Rochester","University of Wisconsin-Madison","University of Würzburg","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Astrophysics","LIMITS","Monte Carlo","Performance","SEARCH","Scattering","Spectrum"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"icecube high energy starting event sample description and flux characterization with 000000000007 000000000005 years of data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/276327528/PhysRevD.104.022002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-545941","identifie