{"abstract":"In multi-messenger astronomy, rapid investigation of interesting transients is imperative. As an observatory with a 4 pi steradian field of view, and similar to 99% uptime, the IceCube Neutrino Observatory is a unique facility to follow up transients, as well as to provide valuable insights for other observatories and inform their observational decisions. Since 2016, IceCube has been using low-latency data to rapidly respond to interesting astrophysical events reported by the multi-messenger observational community. Here, we describe the pipeline used to perform these followup analyses, and provide a summary of the 58 analyses performed as of July 2020. We find no significant signal in the first 58 analyses performed. The pipeline has helped inform various electromagnetic observation strategies, and has constrained neutrino emission from potential hadronic cosmic accelerators.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Aartsen, M. G.","Abbasi, R.","Ackermann, M.","Adams, J.","Aguilar, J. A.","Ahlers, Markus Tobias","Ahrens, M.","Alispach, C.","Amin, N. M.","Andeen, K.","Anderson, T.","Ansseau, I.","Anton, G.","Arguelles, C.","Auffenberg, J.","Axani, S.","Bagherpour, H.","Bai, X.","Balagopal, A. V.","Barbano, A.","Barwick, S. W.","Bastian, B.","Basu, V.","Baum, V.","Baur, S.","Bay, R.","Beatty, J. J.","Becker, K. -H.","Tjus, J. Becker","Bellenghi, C.","BenZvi, S.","Berley, D.","Bernardini, E.","Besson, D. Z.","Binder, G.","Bindig, D.","Blaufuss, E.","Blot, S.","Bohm, C.","Boeser, S.","Botner, O.","Boettcher, J.","Bourbeau, Etienne","Bourbeau, J.","Bradascio, F.","Braun, J.","Koskinen, D. Jason","Medici, Morten Ankersen","Rameez, M","Stuttard, Thomas Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416045"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["Icecube Collaboration"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Italy","New Zealand","Russia","Sweden","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DESY, Helmholtz Association, Deutsches Elektronen-Synchrotron (DESY)","Free University of Brussels","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","Harvard University","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Karlsruhe Inst Technol, Helmholtz Association, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Inst Astroparticle Phys","Loyola Univ, Loyola University Chicago, Dept Phys","Marquette University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Moscow Engineering Physics Institute","Ohio State University","RWTH Aachen University","South Dakota Sch Mines & Technol, South Dakota School Mines & Technology, Dept Phys","Stockholm University","Technical University of Munich","Univ Delaware, University of Delaware, Dept Phys & Astron","Univ Wuppertal, University of Wuppertal, Dept Phys","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Irvine","University of Canterbury","University of Geneva","University of Maryland, College Park","University of Padua","University of Rochester","University of Wisconsin-Madison","University of Würzburg","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["High energy astrophysics","Neutrino astronomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"follow up of astrophysical transients in real time with the icecube neutrino observatory","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.04577.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-416045","identifier":[{"id":"85103613997","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000631359100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-25d322ac-1474-45f2-9533-a8b7360293f3"],"keyword":["High energy astrophysics","Neutrino astronomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["G