":"Kasper Tang","key":"vangkildeped","last":"Vangkilde","locid":"f9d45064-7c54-4c5e-81a1-db34e797920e","name":"Vangkilde, Kasper Tang","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kasper Tang","key":"vangkildepau","last":"Vangkilde","locid":"2ceefaea-2b51-4c19-8279-ca7107323706","name":"Vangkilde, Kasper Tang","orcid":"0000-0002-0971-2827","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Gislev","key":"kjærsgaardped","last":"Kjærsgaard","locid":"4302b41b-5117-407b-9b29-597c5fb0a791","name":"Kjærsgaard, Mette Gislev","orcid":"0000-0001-7978-1943","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ton","key":"ottoped","last":"Otto","locid":"90fe48d1-ca66-4f68-81e3-fd48f0fa67b6","name":"Otto, Ton","orcid":"0000-0002-5185-3017","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joachim","key":"halseped","last":"Halse","locid":"9a535e7b-a08a-4ed5-a30b-1e45d477dfa5","name":"Halse, Joachim","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"binderped","last":"Binder","locid":"c74da6b3-52d3-4ac5-9078-0921bcae572c","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":6,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781874280600"],"isbn":["9781474280600","1474280609"],"pages":"304","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-401576a0-0e5f-4608-9f1a-b14ed8ddd6d0","au-c6899753-7e23-40c7-88fe-bb82b61cea21","ku-a3e1c8d3-8324-405c-874b-c22c3eb69e26","sdu-7e08fb3e-b449-401a-949a-add031821626"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Design Anthropological Futures","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-093.55-012383","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Samarbejde, samskabelse og social nysgerrighed er i dag en præmis for den nyskabende designer. Det sociale er det nye designmateriale som unge designere giver sig i kast med når f.eks. Emmy Linde samarbejder med plejehjemsbeboere, deres pårørende, plejepersonale og fysioterapeuter for at designe trygge og oplevelsesrige gangruter for demente i Næstved. Hvad vil motivere til at gå tur, og hvad vil det sige at være tryg i det offentlige rum som dement? Emmy fulgte hverdagen på et plejehjem. Hun afholdt workshops, der tog udgangspunkt i sanserne, og lavede eksperimenter i 1:1, hvor uderum, der inviterer til aktivitet og ’wayfinding’ gradvist tog form gennem afprøvning og dialog. Denne designpraksis kaldes ’kollaborativ design’ eller i kort form ’codesign’. Men hvad er godt design med ’det sociale’ som designmateriale? Og hvad er vedkommende samtidsdesign når designere og designstuderende slipper de faste holdepunkter i studiokulturen og den kanon for dansk design som mange ser det som en vigtig opgave at være kurator for? Det er nogle af de spørgsmål som kapitlet kredse om.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brandt, Eva","Binder, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-127959"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Codesign","Social innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"med det sociale som designmateriale","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-127959","ids":["arkc-b4d06f14-0b9d-4bf3-abef-a43b40e05a75"],"keyword":["Ja","codesign","design-maker","det sociale som designmateriale","samtidsdesign","social innovation"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8DB7568207CC7AA4BE0F2EF37FAAB107"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Design","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Design, Institute of Product Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"4186dd98-15a8-4d67-a630-5d0875e85920","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c74da6b3-52d3-4ac5-9078-0921bcae572c","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"dybdahlpedh","last":"Dybdahl","name":"Dybdahl, Lars","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788792949431"],"pages":"354-361","place":"København","publisher":"Strandberg Publishing","status":"p","title":"Dansk Design Nu","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-b4d06f14-0b9d-4bf3-abef-a43b40e05a75"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Med det sociale som designmateriale","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-127959","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Design Anthropological Futures explores futures and future-making from a design anthropological perspective. Here futures are not understood as striking visions created and implemented by scientists or designers, but rather as collaborative explorations of situated possibilities, formations and actions at the intersection of design and everyday life. The term futures relates both to the theoretical and practical engagement of design anthropology with futures and future-making as a subject – futures in design anthropology – and to the exploration of possible future directions for the discipline itself through such engagements – futures of design anthropology. Through various design anthropological investigations at specific sites – from care homes to corporate organizations, eco-homes to museums, Rio de Janeiro to Italy – this book critically addresses a number of dominant perspectives on, and approaches to, futures, including implied assumptions of singularity, linearity, locality and novelty. In the following we briefly elaborate on these themes and propose alternative perspectives for a design anthropological approach to futures.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Kjærsgaard, Mette Gislev","Halse, Joachim","Smith, Rachel Charlotte","Vangkilde, Kasper Tang","Binder, Thomas","Otto, Ton"],"cuid":["S02-091.84-767315"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction design anthropological futures","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","