:"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Alicia K","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27717399"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-016-1068-z","issn":["14747596","1474760X"],"issn_org":["14747596"],"issue":"1","journal":"Genome Biology","pages":"206","paperid":"206","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Genome Biology","title_org":"Genome Biology (Online Edition)","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84990848178"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-64135a83-2b67-4b77-a514-a53827e4e0ac","ku-921d9643-0a7a-4bb3-96c9-b06b610a787c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An epigenetic clock for gestational age at birth based on blood methylation data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.68-019945","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In a competing risks setting, the cumulative incidence of an event of interest describes the absolute risk for this event as a function of time. For regression analysis, one can either choose to model all competing events by separate cause-specific hazard models or directly model the association between covariates and the cumulative incidence of one of the events. With a suitable link function, direct regression models allow for a straightforward interpretation of covariate effects on the cumulative incidence. In practice, where data can be right-censored, these regression models are implemented using a pseudo-value approach. For a grid of time points, the possibly unobserved binary event status is replaced by a jackknife pseudo-value based on the Aalen-Johansen method. We combine a stagewise regression technique with the pseudo-value approach to provide variable selection while allowing for time-varying effects. This is implemented by coupling variable selection between the grid times, but determining estimates separately. The effect estimates are regularized to also allow for model fitting with a low to moderate number of observations. This technique is illustrated in an application using clinical cancer registry data from hepatocellular carcinoma patients. The results are contrasted with traditional hazard-based modeling. In addition to a more straightforward interpretation, when using the proposed technique, the identification of time-varying effect patterns on the cumulative incidence is seen to be feasible with a moderate number of observations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zöller, Daniela","Schmidtmann, Irene","Weinmann, Arndt","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Binder, Harald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434625"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stagewise pseudo value regression for time varying effects on the cumulative incidence","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-434625","identifier":[{"id":"84959480849","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26510388","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-44f96c1f-aa62-4452-80f7-4a53ad0b5b5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE90A791471378A330B63B709425BB75"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Daniela","key":"zöllerpau","last":"Zöller","name":"Zöller, Daniela","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Irene","key":"schmidtmannpau","last":"Schmidtmann","name":"Schmidtmann, Irene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arndt","key":"weinmannpau","last":"Weinmann","name":"Weinmann, Arndt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas A.","key":"gerdspau","last":"Gerds","locid":"b87ed711-194a-48dc-b83a-3c7aad18a00d","name":"Gerds, Thomas Alexander","name_org":"Gerds, Thomas A.","orcid":"0000-0002-5955-816X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Harald","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Harald","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26510388"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/sim.6770","issn":["02776715","10970258"],"issn_org":["02776715"],"issue":"7","journal":"Statistics in Medicine","pages":"1144-1158","status":"p","title":"Statistics in Medicine","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959480849"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-44f96c1f-aa62-4452-80f7-4a53ad0b5b5f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stagewise pseudo-value regression for time-varying effects on the cumulative incidence","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434625","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
