{"abstract":"For more than four decades participatory design has provided exemplars and concepts for understanding the democratic potential of design participation. Despite important impacts on design methodology participatory design has however been stuck in a marginal position as it has wrestled with what has been performed and accomplished in participatory practices. In this article we discuss how participatory design may be reinvigorated as a design research programme for democratic design experiments in the light of the de-centring of human-centredness and the foregrounding of collaborative representational practices offered by the ANT tradition in the tension between a parliament of things and a laboratory of circulating references.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Binder, Thomas","Brandt, Eva","Ehn, Pelle","Halse, Joachim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-127240"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Democracy","Experiment","Laboratory","Parliament","Participation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"democratic design experiments between parliament and laboratory","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/15710882.2015.1081248","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-127240","identifier":[{"id":"84946484862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-7981c492-4443-4474-96a7-9b6d25d12dff"],"keyword":["No","democracy","experiment","laboratory","parliament","participation","thing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32426108892F600AD6F4AF64BDADF19F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Design, Institute of Design and Visual Interaction, CODE - Centre for Codesign"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c74da6b3-52d3-4ac5-9078-0921bcae572c","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"4186dd98-15a8-4d67-a630-5d0875e85920","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pelle","key":"ehnpau","last":"Ehn","name":"Ehn, Pelle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joachim","key":"halsepau","last":"Halse","locid":"9a535e7b-a08a-4ed5-a30b-1e45d477dfa5","name":"Halse, Joachim","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15710882","17453755"],"issn_org":["15710882"],"issue":"3-4","journal":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","pages":"152-165","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","title_org":"CoDesign","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946484862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-7981c492-4443-4474-96a7-9b6d25d12dff"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Democratic design experiments: between parliament and laboratory","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-127240","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Association studies have greatly refined the understanding of how variation within the human leukocyte antigen (HLA) genes influences risk of multiple sclerosis. However, the extent to which major effects are modulated by interactions is poorly characterized. We analyzed high-density SNP data on 17,465 cases and 30,385 controls from 11 cohorts of European ancestry, in combination with imputation of classical HLA alleles, to build a high-resolution map of HLA genetic risk and assess the evidence for interactions involving classical HLA alleles. Among new and previously identified class II risk alleles (HLA-DRB1*15:01, HLA-DRB1*13:03, HLA-DRB1*03:01, HLA-DRB1*08:01 and HLA-DQB1*03:02) and class I protective alleles (HLA-A*02:01, HLA-B*44:02, HLA-B*38:01 and HLA-B*55:01), we find evidence for two interactions involving pairs of class II alleles: HLA-DQA1*01:01-HLA-DRB1*15:01 and HLA-DQB1*03:01-HLA-DQB1*03:02. We find no evidence for interactions between classical HLA alleles and non-HLA risk-associated variants and estimate a minimal effect of polygenic epistasis in modulating major risk alleles.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Moutsianas, Loukas","Jostins, Luke","Beecham, Ashley H","Dilthey, Alexander T","Xifara, Dionysia K","Ban, Maria","Shah, Tejas S","Patsopoulos, Nikolaos A","Alfredsson, Lars","Anderson, Carl A","Attfield, Katherine E","Baranzini, Sergio E","Barrett, Jeffrey","Binder, Thomas M C","Booth, David","Buck, Dorothea","Celius, Elisabeth G","Cotsapas, Chris","D'Alfonso, Sandra","Dendrou, Calliope A","Donnelly, Peter","Dubois, Bénédicte","Fontaine, Bertrand","Lar Fugger, Lars","Goris, An","Gourraud, Pierre-Antoine","Graetz, Christiane","Hemmer, Bernhard","Hillert, Jan","Kockum, Ingrid","Leslie, Stephen","Lill, Christina M","Martinelli-Boneschi, Filippo","Oksenberg, Jorge R","Olsson, Tomas","Oturai, Annette Bang","Saarela, Janna","Sondergaard, Helle Bach","Spurkland, Anne","Taylor, Bruce","Winkelmann, Juliane","Zipp, Frauke","Haines, Jonathan L","Pericak-Vance, Margaret A","Spencer, Chris C A","Stewart, Graeme","Hafler, David A","Ivinson, Adrian J","Harbo, Hanne F","Hauser, Stephen L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["International IBD Genetics Consortium (IIBDGC)"],"keyword":["Alleles","Epistasis Genetic","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Histocompatibility Antigens Class II","Humans","Multiple sclerosis","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"class ii hla interactions modulate genetic risk for multiple sclerosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-444118","identifier":[{"id":"84942981489","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4874245","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26343388","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-54cf02b8-c3ce-4d76-82fd-2af18bb492e1"],"keyword":["Alleles","Epistasis, Genetic","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Histocompatibility Antigens Class II","Humans","Multiple Sclerosis","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-218A8C701692813ED96910ED683842CD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"international ibd genetics consortium","name":"International IBD Genetics C