{"abstract":"Design experiments are powerful inquiries, working from the ambiguous and tentative to more firm programmatic statements. In participatory design and codesign, learning and knowing is closely tied to participation − the engagement with and manipulation of shared representations, as participants expose how they become knowledgeable in what they collaboratively make. However, working with codesign as an integral part of knowledge production poses challenges to how we conceive of such inquiries in the practices of research through design. This paper reports from collaborative research where fellow researchers and PhD students carry out a codesign experiment (in the Xlab meta-project). The intention of the paper is twofold but intertwined: to get closer at what it is that people actually do in a codesign experiment situation; and to further investigate the relationship between program and experiments. We will give examples of the considerations and crises faced by the participants and how they try to solve them. In addition, we suggest using the notion of ‘sub-program’ as a way of describing the framing of a specific experiment thus adding to the program-experiment dialectics in the designing and doing of experiments.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Brandt, Eva","Eriksen, Mette Agger","Binder, Thomas","Redström, Johan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126065"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-04","place":"Brisbane, au","start":"2015-11-01","title":"IASDR 2015 Interplay","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Experiment","Knowledge production"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the perform codesign experiment on what people actually do and the relation between program and experiment in research through design","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/58822598/Brandt_et_al_IASDR15_The_Perform_experiment_FINAL_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126065","ids":["arkc-113a5a5f-50f7-4c75-9538-6124fca34daf"],"keyword":["No","designing codesign experiments","experiment","experiments/program dialectics","knowledge production","meta-reflections","research program","sub-program"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-141AB48D5AD46A6AD3DD4CC46562AF6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://iasdr2015.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/IASDR_Proceedings_Final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/58822598/Brandt_et_al_IASDR15_The_Perform_experiment_FINAL_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Design","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Design, Institute of Product Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"4186dd98-15a8-4d67-a630-5d0875e85920","name":"Brandt, Eva","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Agger","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Mette Agger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c74da6b3-52d3-4ac5-9078-0921bcae572c","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"redströmpau","last":"Redström","name":"Redström, Johan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vesna","key":"popovicetalpedh","last":"Popovic et al","name":"Popovic et al, Vesna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780646943183"],"pages":"234-249","place":"Brisbane, Australia","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings Publication","title":"IASDR 2015 Interplay"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-113a5a5f-50f7-4c75-9538-6124fca34daf"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"The Perform Codesign Experiment – on what people actually do and the relation between program and experiment in research through design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126065","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
