{"abstract":"Regression analysis for competing risks data can be based on generalized estimating equations. For the case with right censored data, pseudo-values were proposed to solve the estimating equations. In this article we investigate robustness of the pseudo-values against violation of the assumption that the probability of not being lost to follow-up (un-censored) is independent of the covariates. Modified pseudo-values are proposed which rely on a correctly specified regression model for the censoring times. Bias and efficiency of these methods are compared in a simulation study. Further illustration of the differences is obtained in an application to bone marrow transplantation data and a corresponding sensitivity analysis.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Binder, Nadine","Gerds, Thomas Alexander","Andersen, Per Kragh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-484460"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pseudo observations for competing risks with covariate dependent censoring","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10985-013-9247-7","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-484460","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4573528","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84897065476","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23430270","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-98434cb5-b93f-40d3-911a-6a6a8d5be637"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5AC8BF9F48E5879780CD1C9CD1A71E5D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10985-013-9247-7","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":