{"abstract":"Neurosteroids are synthesized both in brain and peripheral steroidogenic tissue from cholesterol or steroidal precursors. Neurosteroids have been shown to be implicated in neural proliferation, differentiation, and activity. Preclinical and clinical studies also suggest a modulatory role of neurosteroids in anxiety-related phenotypes. However, little is known about the contribution of genetic variants in genes relevant for the neurosteroidogenesis to anxiety disorders.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Quast, Carina","Reif, Andreas","Brückl, Tanja","Pfister, Hildegard","Weber, Heike","Mattheisen, Manuel","Cichon, Sven","Lang, Thomas","Hamm, Alfons","Fehm, Lydia","Ströhle, Andreas","Arolt, Volker","Domschke, Katharina","Kircher, Tilo","Wittchen, Hans-Ulrich","Pauli, Paul","Gerlach, Alexander L","Alpers, Georg W","Deckert, Jürgen","Rupprecht, Rainer","Binder, Elisabeth B","Erhardt, Angelika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-176230"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Psychiatry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender specific association of variants in the akr000000000001c000000000001 gene with dimensional anxiety in patients with panic disorder additional evidence for the importance of neurosteroids in anxiety","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/da.22229","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-176230","identifier":[{"id":"24390875","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84914665976","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-522e0032-4e11-49aa-9dbf-5f925f43bead"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Scien