u","last":"Tong","name":"Tong, Weida","rank":159,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David P.","key":"kreildavidppau","last":"Kreil","name":"Kreil, David P.","rank":160,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher E.","key":"masonchristopherepau","last":"Mason","name":"Mason, Christopher E.","rank":161,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Leming","key":"shilemingpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Leming","rank":162,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25150838"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/nbt.2957","issn":["10870156","15461696"],"issn_org":["10870156"],"issue":"9","journal":"Nature Biotechnology","pages":"903-914","status":"p","title":"Nature Biotechnology","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920550975"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1e0fbe7d-d34e-4b83-ad09-9db324d3056b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A comprehensive assessment of RNA-seq accuracy, reproducibility and information content by the Sequencing Quality Control Consortium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-411307","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this presentation I will try to get hold of some very special moments that have become almost an obsession for me in my work with what my colleagues and I call the design laboratory. These very special moments are not some that we can easily stage and though we have experienced them again and again they always come as a surprise and with a deep feeling of fulfillment. One of such moments arrived in the middle of an intense design research project where we were a group of colleagues working for the Sony Ericsson company to educate their UX team in codesign approaches to user research. Together with a small network of mobile phone users we had explored the everyday transition going to work and returning back home. We had played design games with visual materials gathered through our participation in these transitions and together we had enacted a small series of fictional video stories about how we imagined mobile phones in the future. At the end of one of the first workshops our small research group was gathering and one of my colleagues very nicely summed up one of those moments I am talking about, by saying that now it is like the lid has come off and everything is possible. What he pointed to was not (solely) a sense of alignment with the company or our user collaborators, nor was it (just) a feeling of knowing how to bring the project successfully to an end. It was a more specific experience of being at a point where the design and use of possible future mobile phones was no longer a blind search for openings in the company product strategy (or for that sake in the mundaneness of established user practices), but instead a completely open and contingent landscape unfolding in front of us. It is such moments of encountering the possible that I will address in the following, and though the remark of my colleague may well be seen as a reflextive thought on what had just passed, I will try to show that these moments are not moments of reflection or “breakdown” but rather moments of flow and becoming that bring different worlds within reach. I will however start with a brief introduction to the design research practice that we call the design laboratory.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Binder, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126293"],"event":{"end":"2014-04-11","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2014-04-10","title":"Research Network for Design Anthropology","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co design","Design","UX","User experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design laboratories as everyday theater encountering the possible","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://kadk.dk/sites/default/files/10._binder_2014_design_laboratories_as_everyday_theater.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126293","ids":["arkc-248152a2-1c81-4e52-8a56-e85592f4b4ae"],"keyword":["Design","Nej","UX","User Experience","co-design"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6ED677612CE3CCE2C9D6AD1A197C8636"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://kadk.dk/sites/default/files/10._binder_2014_design_laboratories_as_everyday_theater.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Design"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c74da6b3-52d3-4ac5-9078-0921bcae572c","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-248152a2-1c81-4e52-8a56-e85592f4b4ae"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Design Laboratories as Everyday Theater : Encountering the Possible","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126293","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The distinction between design and use is getting blurred in several ways as products and services increasingly are co-created in use, and use and users proliferate and diversify. This has led to a growing interest in staging what we here will call design laboratories that both involve future users in codesign and incubate emergent everyday practices of design in use. In this panel that brings together researchers from some of the environments that most vigorously has pursued this line of inquiry we will ask what it is that constitutes a successful design laboratory and what we can expect design laboratories to accomplish in a world of diversity.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Binder, Thomas","Malmborg, Lone","Hillgren, Per-Anders","Messeter, Jörn","Lee, Yanki","Thinyane, Mamello"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381967"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-06","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2013-09-02","title":"14th International Conference on INTERACT","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Hong Kong","South Africa","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University","The Hong Kong Polytechnic University","University of Fort Hare"],"keyword":["Co design","Community","Living labs","Open innovation","Participation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"OT":["Danish Center for Design Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what can design laboratories do","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.irit.fr/recherches/ICS/events/conferences/interact2013/papers/8120774.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381967","ids":["itu-2f50bd4b-87e8-4de1-97bf-3f6ee679c0d7"],"keyword":["Co-design","Community","Living labs","Open innovation","Participation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8A0F8BC137BF79538C55EBC84D72F7A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.irit.fr/recherches/ICS/events/conferences/interact2013/papers/8120774.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Center for Design Research"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"hk","key":"the hong kong polytechnic university","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The Hong Kong Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"za","key":"university of fort hare","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of Fort Hare","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Per-Anders","key":"hillgrenpau","last":"Hillgren","name":"Hillgren, Per-Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"messeterpau","last":"Messeter","locid":"a4c1604d-b01f-46ef-baf3-74d2a8046d6b","name":"Messeter, Jörn","orcid":"0000-0002-2181-149X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanki","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Yanki","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Mamello","key":"thinyanepau","last":"Thinyane","name":"Thinyane, Mamello","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2f50bd4b-87e8-4de1-97bf-3f6ee679c0d7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What can Design Laboratories do?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381967","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The immunoglobulins expressed by chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) B cells are highly restricted, suggesting they are selected for binding either self or foreign antigen. Of the immunoglobulin heavy-chain variable (IGHV) genes expressed in CLL, IGHV1-69 is the most common, and often is expressed with little or no somatic mutation, and restricted IGHD and IGHJ gene usage. We found that antibodies encoded by one particular IGHV1-69 subset, designated CLL69C, with the HCDR3 encoded by the IGHD3-3 gene in reading frame 2 and IGHJ6, specifically bound to oxidation-specific epitopes (OSE), which are products of enhanced lipid peroxidation and a major target of innate natural antibodies. Specifically, CLL69C bound immunodominant OSE adducts termed MAA (malondialdehyde-acetaldehyde-adducts), which are found on apoptotic cells, inflammatory tissues, and atherosclerotic lesions. It also reacted specifically with MAA-specific peptide mimotopes. Light chain shuffling indicated that non-stochastically paired L chain of IGLV3-9 contributes to the antigen binding of CLL69C. A nearly identical CLL69C Ig heavy chain was identified from an MAA-enriched umbilical cord phage displayed Fab library, and a derived Fab with the same HCDR3 rearrangement displayed identical MAA-binding properties. These data support the concept that OSE (MAA-epitopes), which are ubiquitous products of inflammation, may play a role in clonal selection and expansion of CLL B cells.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Que, Xuchu","Widhopf Ii, George F","Amir, Shahzada","Hartvigsen, Karsten","Hansen, Lotte F","Woelkers, Douglas","Tsimikas, Sotirios","Binder, Christoph J","Kipps, Thomas J","Witztum, Joseph L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477636"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ighv000000000001 000000000069 encoded antibodies expressed in chronic lymphocytic leukemia react with malondialdehyde acetaldehyde adduct an immunodominant oxidation specific epitope","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0065203","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-477636","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3688726","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23840319","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84879255556","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8cccf966-3948-4e4e-a113-d1b4d045c118"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BB1E4413A954FBA89228FB8BCE31EA8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0065203","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Xuchu","key":"quepau","last":"Que","name":"Que, Xuchu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"George F","key":"widhopfiipau","last":"Widhopf Ii","name":"Widhopf Ii, George F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shahzada","key":"amirpau","last":"Amir","name":"Amir, Shahzada","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karsten","key":"hartvigsenpau","last":"Hartvigsen","locid":"6a2fe0dc-01c4-4c9d-ab85-0453fb06fe14","name":"Hartvigsen, Karsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lotte F","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lotte F","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Douglas","key":"woelkerspau","last":"Woelkers","name":"Woelkers, Douglas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sotirios","key":"tsimikaspau","last":"Tsimikas","name":"Tsimikas, Sotirios","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoph J","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Christoph J","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas J","key":"kippspau","last":"Kipps","name":"Kipps, Thomas J","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joseph L","key":"witztumpau","last":"Witztum","name":"Witztum, Joseph L","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23840319"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0065203","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"6","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879255556"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8cccf966-3948-4e4e-a113-d1b4d045c118"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"IGHV1-69-Encoded Antibodies Expressed in Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia React with Malondialdehyde-Acetaldehyde Adduct, an Immunodominant Oxidation-Specific Epitope","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477636","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Most psychiatric disorders are moderately to highly heritable. The degree to which genetic variation is unique to individual disorders or shared across disorders is unclear. To examine shared genetic etiology, we use genome-wide genotype data from the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium (PGC) for cases and controls in schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder, autism spectrum disorders (ASD) and attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD). We apply univariate and bivariate methods for the estimation of genetic variation within and covariation between disorders. SNPs explained 17-29% of the variance in liability. The genetic correlation calculated using common SNPs was high between schizophrenia and bipolar disorder (0.68 ± 0.04 s.e.), moderate between schizophrenia and major depressive disorder (0.43 ± 0.06 s.e.), bipolar disorder and major depressive disorder (0.47 ± 0.06 s.e.), and ADHD and major depressive disorder (0.32 ± 0.07 s.e.), low between schizophrenia and ASD (0.16 ± 0.06 s.e.) and non-significant for other pairs of disorders as well as between psychiatric disorders and the negative control of Crohn's disease. This empirical evidence of shared genetic etiology for psychiatric disorders can inform nosology and encourages the investigation of common pathophysiologies for related disorders.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Lee, S Hong","Ripke, Stephan","Neale, Benjamin M","Faraone, Stephen V","Purcell, Shaun M","Perlis, Roy H","Mowry, Bryan J","Thapar, Anita","Goddard, Michael E","Witte, John S","Absher, Devin","Agartz, Ingrid","Akil, Huda","Amin, Farooq","Andreassen, Ole A","Anjorin, Adebayo","Anney, Richard","Anttila, Verneri","Arking, Dan E","Asherson, Philip","Azevedo, Maria H","Backlund, Lena","Badner, Judith A","Bailey, Anthony J","Banaschewski, Tobias","Barchas, Jack D","Barnes, Michael R","Barrett, Thomas B","Bass, Nicholas","Battaglia, Agatino","Bauer, Michael","Bayés, Mònica","Bellivier, Frank","Bergen, Sarah E","Berrettini, Wade","Betancur, Catalina","Bettecken, Thomas","Biederman, Joseph","Binder, Elisabeth B","Black, Donald W","Blackwood, Douglas H R","Bloss, Cinnamon S","Boehnke, Michael","Boomsma, Dorret I","Breen, Gerome","Breuer, René","Bruggeman, Richard","Cormican, Paul","Mattheisen, Manuel","Meier, Sandra"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008428"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Cross-Disorder Group of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic relationship between five psychiatric disorders estimated from genome wide snps","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2711","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-008428","identifier":[{"id":"23933821","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84883465830","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000323748200007","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC3800159","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-aee58528-2843-48fd-b9c4-3d156d28e6e2","au-9d5460a9-3466-44d7-9e10-0ea5b33a89c0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3B5FF7F7EAA6773CAAB8CCC2F23EC082"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.2711","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bar